cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
title: "Applied Natural Language Processing: From Tokens to Agents"
abstract: >-
  A free, hands-on book on modern natural language processing, written for
  engineers outside computer science and for statistics students, and taken
  from a live course at METU (ODTU), Ankara. It runs from tokenization and
  bag-of-words through transformers, LLM techniques, and agentic systems.
  Every number in the book is measured rather than quoted, and Turkish is
  used throughout as a stress test for tools tuned on English. Published in
  two independent editions, English and Turkish.
